From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:40:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A play connection's frames are split, inflated and decoded in
 one handler

Each frame went through three ByteToMessageDecoders, each with its output list,
cumulation, slice and serializer: 5% of a match's CPU (VPS-B, 8 rooms, ~110 players
over the network). With the server's own decompressor and decoder right after it, the
splitter reads the frame where it lies and passes the packet on from the decoder's
place. Anything else in between, the 1.7 translator, or another protocol takes the
three stages. -Dathena.disableDirectDecode=true turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

